{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>To a land flowing with milk and honey.</b> It follows from this that this is a desolate place, and you need to be sustained in it by a miracle for which you are not worthy — therefore go to a land flowing with milk and honey, where you will be able to be sustained without a miracle." "<b>For I will not go up in your midst.</b> Therefore I say: עֲלֵה מִזֶּה אַתָּה וְהָעָם (Exodus 33:1), and do not wait to encamp and journey at HaShem's word, for I will not go up in your midst." "<b>Lest I consume you on the way.</b> For when I dwell in your midst, the punishment for your sins will be greater."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:52.054017886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}